<title>COLOMBIA: Colombian govt sells stakes in two power plants.</title>
<headline>Colombian govt sells stakes in two power plants.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Colombian government sold its 99 percent stake in the Betania power plant to Chilean company Endesa-Colombia for 302 billion pesos Thursday, officials said.</p>
<p>It sold its 14.25 percent stake in the Termocartagena power plant for 2 billion pesos to the Venezuelan consortium Electricidad Caracas, the official said.</p>
</text>
